# Munich Expo Hackathon — .gitignore
#
# Stack-agnostic on purpose: the stack is undecided (see
# design/decisions/ADR-0002-stack-selection.md). This file intentionally does NOT commit to
# Python/Node/etc-specific build-artifact ignores yet; whoever resolves that ADR should extend
# this file in the same change as the canonical commands + smoke test.
#
# IMPORTANT — this repo will later be grafted onto the agent-bus multi-agent protocol, which
# expects test fixtures under tests/ to be trackable. Do NOT add blanket data-file patterns here
# (bare *.csv, *.json, *.parquet, data/, etc.) — `git add` silently skips ignored files, so a
# fixture that only exists on disk passes locally and fails in CI. If a future edit to this file
# adds such a pattern, it MUST be paired with a `!tests/**` (or narrower) negation immediately
# after it. See the negation guard at the bottom of this file.

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor/IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Env / secrets — never commit real credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generic working/scratch areas (directory-level whitelist: keep the dir's own README/.gitignore
# tracked, ignore everything else placed inside it)
logs/*
!logs/README.md
!logs/.gitignore
scratch/*
!scratch/.gitignore

# --- Safety-net negation guard for tests/ fixtures ---
# Whatever gets ignored above (or added above in the future), never let it swallow anything under
# tests/. This is a deliberate belt-and-suspenders re-inclusion, not evidence a broad pattern
# exists above yet — it's here pre-emptively because this repo grafts onto agent-bus later.
!tests/**
